{title: Man of Constant Sorrow}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
[G]I am a [C]man of constant [G]sorrow,
I've [G]seen trouble [D7]all my [G]days.
I [G]bid fare[C]well to old Ken[G]tucky,
The [G]place where [D7]I was born and [G]raised.

{c: Verse 2}
[G]For six long [C]years I've been in [G]trouble,
No [G]pleasure [D7]here on earth I [G]found.
For [G]in this [C]world I'm bound to [G]ramble,
I [G]have no [D7]friends to help me [G]now.

{c: Verse 3}
[G]It's fare you [C]well, my own true [G]lover,
I [G]never ex[D7]pect to see you a[G]gain.
For [G]I'm bound to [C]ride that northern [G]railroad,
Per[G]haps I'll [D7]die upon this [G]train.
